# =============================================================================
# .env.example   (agent)
# =============================================================================
# PURPOSE: A template for agent/.env, which holds the Gemini secrets. Commit
# THIS file, but NEVER commit .env (it's in .gitignore).
#
# WHAT TO BUILD: Under the TODOs below, add 3 lines in the form NAME=value,
# without "#". Leave the values blank in this example file, and put the real
# values in your own .env.
#
# TALKS TO: main.py loads .env with python-dotenv (load_dotenv()).
#           gemini_agent.py reads GEMINI_API_KEY and GEMINI_MODEL with
#           os.getenv(...).
#
# STEPS:
#   1. GEMINI_API_KEY=
#        A free key from Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey).
#        It lives ONLY here. Not in server/, and never in client/.
#   2. GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
#        Switch to a newer Flash model when one is available.
#   3. AGENT_PORT=8000
#        The port the agent runs on. It must match AGENT_URL in server/.env.
#   4. Copy this file to agent/.env and fill in the real values.
#
# CONCEPTS TO LEARN:
#   - Environment variables (os.getenv)
#   - python-dotenv (load_dotenv)
# =============================================================================

GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
AGENT_PORT=8000
